comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T13:11:29.225Z",codex-sol,"Reusing this CI capacity Task for Fleet CI v2, companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve all four required checks (test 22/26 and Windows launcher 22/26). One quick Node 26 npm release gate per PR replaces four full gates, removing sequential gate accumulation implicated in #154. Deep keeps all four full gates as isolated matrix jobs. Keep the 20 GiB guard and all coverage thresholds. Release caller rollout pm-ops#272 files are out of scope."
  "2026-11-15T13:18:12.191Z",codex-sol,"Latest successful main run 43609609072: test 22 execution 176m30s, test 26 93m03s; each ran npm and Bun gates. CLI combined-log download returned empty; direct jobs API log supplied evidence. Slowest lifecycle model 835s; large-history and exhaustive crash matrices also dominate. Added deterministic quick prefixes, propagated depth/time-scale through the child allowlist, scaled crash subprocess safety budgets and replaced the 512 TiB refusal speed assertion with a one-read bound. Existing annotation managed fixtures already await owned resources and retry removal (maxRetries 8); #151 is regression verification, not a newly reproduced fix. Coverage thresholds and all old gate contracts retained. Local quick coverage deferred because exhaustive matrices and historical runtime make the 20-minute budget implausible."
  "2026-11-15T13:19:19.949Z",codex-sol,"Strict YAML parsing with unique-key validation passed for all three tier workflows; actionlint is unavailable. Source typecheck, build, duplicates (0%), docstrings (616 declarations) and lint pass. Initial build:test ran before dist existed and failed on three pre-existing dist imports; source build has completed and the linked check is rerunning. Bounded focused quick tests and existing ENOTEMPTY lifecycle regressions are running."
